#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092089 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/id #uuid "0d1dcc59-e7af-5a86-87ba-aa7ee1b23767" :question/math-academy-id "e-632" :question/problem "Find the area bounded by the polar curve $r = \\cos(3\\theta)$ and the lines $\\theta = -\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ and $\\theta = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}.$\n\n![](images/35/350a721c254dab3a8acb2ae54ca5be0bcde6ab036e6936939194c57ae55fe4ff.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} r^2(\\theta) \\, \\textrm{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta) = \\cos(3\\theta),$ $\\theta_1=-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6},$ and $\\theta_2=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6},$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\theta {|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ){|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}((\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}))+\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092090 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/id #uuid "6040d180-ed1d-52b8-809c-b5820352d3d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-633" :question/problem "Find the area bounded by the polar curve $r = 1+2\\cos\\theta$ for $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3} \\leq \\theta \\leq \\dfrac{4\\pi}{3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/6b/6bfa0990b560bcb09f2a9eb0b9542296f2a8f1c196b6740702e81c59941d66c5.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} r^2(\\theta) \\, \\textrm{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta) = 1+2\\cos(\\theta),$ $\\theta_1=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3},$ and $\\theta_2=\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3},$ this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}(1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+2\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -4\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -3\\sqrt{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092105 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/id #uuid "a2d8dca5-a0f3-5b6f-81f5-4eea46ee70d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-6822" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d7b39805131dc562e233d49a84f69d30e80ca29cb9443012032d18fdb4512054.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r = 2\\sin\\theta + 2\\cos\\theta$ for $\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\leq \\theta \\leq \\dfrac{3\\pi}{4},$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} r^2(\\theta) \\, \\textrm{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta) = 2\\sin\\theta + 2\\cos\\theta,$ $\\theta_1=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ and $\\theta_2=\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4},$ this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(4+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}) \\\\  & =2\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi -2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "773ffc42-e2cb-572a-9030-e9a10ba881ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi +24}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528576} {:answer/id #uuid "a1bcdf62-382b-5121-8803-109ccdad8245" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528689} {:answer/id #uuid "a5649c91-b6ce-5e11-a61e-4473ca3b44bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi -9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528700} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b16dc0-ef14-5998-aff3-022fa9ad94bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi +72}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528711} {:answer/id #uuid "b1addd5e-b739-5991-8970-6b78acd4e746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi -72}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1addd5e-b739-5991-8970-6b78acd4e746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi -72}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528732} :answer-field/id #uuid "870af8e4-9463-5142-8458-8ef364ddaa4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c3c2375-fac6-5465-bbbf-42c39eaebb70" :question/math-academy-id "q-123912" :question/problem "![](images/98/98bc6f2ea4d71368226f0f784d629e98949e07005bc08158206de35a87bea520.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=2\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(9-18\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi })) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}\\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }+\\frac{9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{8}\\,{|}_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}(2\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-9(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))+\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi }{8}-9+\\frac{9}{8}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi -72}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a4bb8c-88f1-5914-b2d5-3312538c815e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(3\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528389} {:answer/id #uuid "32de64f9-d1f2-5273-a235-791a355a3cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528424} {:answer/id #uuid "380fba56-3bbd-5139-8fa0-4225147239fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528442} {:answer/id #uuid "9440c8ed-7f27-549a-8592-91eb673a829c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528652} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e81b37-5a0d-5f3a-a5d2-b8283486c586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5\\theta -9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "380fba56-3bbd-5139-8fa0-4225147239fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528442} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b58951d-0e27-5ba8-8189-e5a72fc144d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2437a359-bd35-5179-92d6-ee80bc33d39e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124357" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the total area enclosed by graph of the polar curve $r=9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9\\theta +5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b4da550-43d1-5bf0-ba07-2d9c8866fa45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi -8}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528557} {:answer/id #uuid "87cb5c61-72c1-5207-ac68-6c4fc40a404e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +8}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528625} {:answer/id #uuid "9c7ba2fb-9f38-56bc-8fe5-e96e6dbabc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +8}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528675} {:answer/id #uuid "a23714c3-4f78-5ba1-a107-d1e73692eea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +4}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528692} {:answer/id #uuid "f974103f-b624-52cf-acc4-f3366c464e19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b4da550-43d1-5bf0-ba07-2d9c8866fa45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi -8}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528557} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d48976e-ecd9-52fe-8371-edaabd05c065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb2c5d25-e3ba-5c5d-9450-482e68e4a749" :question/math-academy-id "q-20640" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a83949bcdf4ed8d99cac451d6db21986c24819d1601578890f86fe3df99666a.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ as shown above." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(4+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =2(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi })) \\\\  & =2(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =3\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =3(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{2})+4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-4+\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -8}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1ffe733-727d-5ca8-9de6-2f0a4144bd80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1ffe733-727d-5ca8-9de6-2f0a4144bd80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528896} :answer-field/id #uuid "451b0468-1ab6-5622-abf5-d01927a565b8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "858e5587-42fe-5f2f-94b7-94758f1a2164" :question/math-academy-id "q-348315" :question/problem "![](images/f3/f33fde62793530cfe8970a9fea690fc71036312483ea617088a8d0a663d5133a.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =(\\theta +\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta )){|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}))+\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0b39530-de5a-5c77-986a-201fc9682d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0b39530-de5a-5c77-986a-201fc9682d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528730} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7cde26-15d1-5ea3-9851-e82954572829" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86ea583e-6e3e-5bb4-93ab-14ccfe18681c" :question/math-academy-id "q-352297" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi +0 \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf4aa39e-778f-58ff-8308-65c8627a83b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf4aa39e-778f-58ff-8308-65c8627a83b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528811} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5704968-f186-54d5-a951-55effb0d3ff9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85d4b81f-f257-5ee9-9249-f54ff8b0fda6" :question/math-academy-id "q-352298" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =2\\pi +0 \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0fa857c-1d3e-5cf2-baa1-2ef2c08c36f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{3}+14\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0fa857c-1d3e-5cf2-baa1-2ef2c08c36f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{3}+14\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528851} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea42cbea-59a6-5df3-b3cd-da64d32d78f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "acc4627b-a75b-5710-8130-818c19bd3eef" :question/math-academy-id "q-352321" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}(3+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}(9+24\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +16{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}(9+24\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +8(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(17\\theta +24\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(17\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}+24\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})+12(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}))+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{3}+12(\\sqrt{3})+2(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{3}+14\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "622acefd-6fc4-5289-acf9-eacb640ce3ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{13\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "622acefd-6fc4-5289-acf9-eacb640ce3ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{13\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528532} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b1fe94c-bcca-5ef1-b698-9fc1476d4a23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63188c95-9ec2-54ce-9302-58600c7d5645" :question/math-academy-id "q-352326" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7ab46adacda52da11a07c783905161c6a6c8ebadb77423d7c70acdb17321a50e.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4+5{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4+\\frac{5(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))}{2}+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{13}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{13}{2}\\theta -\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{13\\pi }{4}+6) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{13\\pi }{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pi +24}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1722fb6a-3828-5c7b-bfd2-cfed88f52b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{\\pi }^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319458} {:answer/id #uuid "04429390-e74b-5e41-90c1-15316c84504e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04429390-e74b-5e41-90c1-15316c84504e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528310} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6b14a60-2547-5577-9014-84c75fd158de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afbc3611-2f90-5c6e-b140-8fc556720700" :question/math-academy-id "q-352330" :question/problem "![](images/32/327f1f7a395616de463c054ec904812dcd422776522a262f956530d3aa9278eb.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }4{\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{\\theta }^{3}}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3})-2(\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33c8c1d5-6245-5e5d-af86-ae89e6d91c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{9\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33c8c1d5-6245-5e5d-af86-ae89e6d91c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{9\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528426} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f185ea2-90bf-5f97-91ff-946b826ac36e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ba92fa4-3450-58d7-9f90-59493b716e4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-352331" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e3f2350ba3651e928c65e1a78908a8f8e93cb690585a3fa16b723d1cf38a5024.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(4+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )}{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{9}{2}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9}{2}\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )}{8}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+4) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{9\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c83586b2-1d92-5d5e-8f6e-4972aca897e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c83586b2-1d92-5d5e-8f6e-4972aca897e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528789} :answer-field/id #uuid "55196b73-4bdb-541d-9f20-8e0ffb0bc727" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d870d48d-9aa5-5918-85fa-03f4b0df3775" :question/math-academy-id "q-352336" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4{\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{\\theta }^{3}}{3}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3})-2(\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a62d9ca-70cf-5bb0-a81d-b44818d65dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528407} {:answer/id #uuid "3baf6327-0772-5626-bef1-153ab2509f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528452} {:answer/id #uuid "604b5f92-c114-511e-a74d-0dc1e2510766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528528} {:answer/id #uuid "d575583a-8ede-5730-b7c0-283f632cd4e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528833} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f01578-2351-567b-8c59-f1220aaa327e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a62d9ca-70cf-5bb0-a81d-b44818d65dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528407} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb2074a7-cded-5820-bd6c-23291aa6aaef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "529c609b-d364-5c28-a5a9-2026822f240a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79626" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the area bounded by graph of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a9f0a47-5957-5b08-aa87-f0e9f9dae695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528409} {:answer/id #uuid "3d1413a7-a029-529d-a86f-b8d38b5b7dff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}{(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528456} {:answer/id #uuid "690e9529-0386-51ce-be2d-a3189387b6fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528551} {:answer/id #uuid "b065bdc2-bb70-5ec7-bdfa-649ce2e20ba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528728} {:answer/id #uuid "b309ec04-8226-537c-b8f0-96608e7c2284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b065bdc2-bb70-5ec7-bdfa-649ce2e20ba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528728} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a7f30de-c83e-5e20-b1c0-29f77397e42d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9bf3624-c382-5070-9fe1-d9a42b576ac0" :question/math-academy-id "q-79793" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the total area enclosed by the graph of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\,$ for $\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4)\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e8e637-7057-5738-bf7e-37e493294f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528302} {:answer/id #uuid "15e653f1-5de1-53ea-abbc-55ef743af9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528354} {:answer/id #uuid "41ba3cc1-a57c-5405-a9a7-4fc4022e386b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528470} {:answer/id #uuid "4c18dc99-1f3e-572b-b474-4613ba1ccc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528490} {:answer/id #uuid "ba5b425b-9a81-5998-a220-805626423f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c18dc99-1f3e-572b-b474-4613ba1ccc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528490} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a913a76-11e5-57cb-aec7-0eda0a258d42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c7bf914-2de6-57ee-85dd-b40dcc8d6cfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-9640" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7ca646111a7708da96fa1bea8aca056abf0c45f9a4295e2beb27181d704aa814.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{8},$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8}+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /8}^{3\\pi /8} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}-\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "460f98e6-2dad-5164-97ed-ca84fd3c06be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528475} {:answer/id #uuid "771fcce6-ddaf-54b3-a739-a6390529f5f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528575} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e72018-e6e3-592b-880f-a6d48f3ebdb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528734} {:answer/id #uuid "b294df79-b64d-5dcb-8a58-b77dd62b8429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528736} {:answer/id #uuid "e6233b81-6983-586a-81cd-f71c40f0288b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1e72018-e6e3-592b-880f-a6d48f3ebdb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528734} :answer-field/id #uuid "4863b9c5-7c52-590c-ac4a-f95a2e691add" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "692ede8e-6241-512f-89fd-e5f23e8be1b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-9641" :question/problem "![](images/ed/ed702f9d982d599fc0f175dc7d7dd022aeefc3f5463aade2a9db71313faf4866.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi })) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(\\pi -0)+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)+\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+0+\\frac{1}{8}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
